usage: flair diffexp [-h] --counts_matrix COUNTS_MATRIX -o OUTPUT [-t THREADS]
                     [--min_expression MIN_EXPRESSION]
                     [--condition_a CONDITION_A] [--condition_b CONDITION_B]
                     [--temp_dir TEMP_DIR] [--keep_intermediate]

Differential expression and differential usage analysis

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -t, --threads THREADS
                        number of threads for parallel DRIMSeq (default: 12)
  --min_expression MIN_EXPRESSION
                        read count expression threshold: a gene or isoform is
                        tested when the reads of at least one condition,
                        summed over its samples, reach this many, and is left
                        out when both conditions have fewer (default: 10)
  --condition_a CONDITION_A
                        the reference condition, as named in the counts matrix
                        columns; fold changes are reported for --condition_b
                        relative to this. With neither this nor --condition_b
                        given, the two conditions are taken in sorted order
  --condition_b CONDITION_B
                        the condition compared against --condition_a
  --temp_dir TEMP_DIR   directory for temporary files; each run makes its own
                        directory, named for the output, in it (default:
                        $TMPDIR or the system temporary directory)
  --keep_intermediate   keep the run's own directory, which holds the tables
                        before filtering and the R scripts' diagnostics, and
                        whose path the run reports

required named arguments:
  --counts_matrix COUNTS_MATRIX
                        tab-delimited isoform count matrix from flair
                        quantify, or the counts of flair spliceevents
                        (OUTPUT.spliceevents.counts.tsv), whose usage only is
                        tested. Conditions and batches are read from the
                        sample info TSV beside it
  -o, --output OUTPUT   output file name base: each table and plot is written
                        as <output>.<name>, as every other subcommand writes
                        its outputs
